Helios DXVK fork: the no-event scanout-acquire signaler idles when nothing is armed

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0015 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

The signaler thread starts on the first armed gate and runs until the device
is destroyed. Without a retirement event it polls the read ledger every 1 ms
holding timeBeginPeriod(1). After about 100 ms of polls with no gate armed it
polls every 10 ms and gives the 1 ms period back; armFence wakes it, and the
next armed gate polls at 1 ms again. A gate counts as armed while its highest
armed value is above the value last signaled: released gates stay in the map
until their claim leaves the ledger, so a non-empty map is not "armed". winmm
is resolved once per thread instead of on every timeBeginPeriod.

armFence re-reads the gate's ledger claim under the signaler mutex and
signals what has retired since the caller sampled the ledger. Without that, a
retirement broadcast between the caller's sample and the gate's creation woke
a signaler pass that had nothing to release yet, and the gate waited for the
next wake (the 10 ms event timeout). The event path is otherwise unchanged.

